INSERT INTO `projects` VALUES (1,'Intersection Collision Avoidance System','Academic','images/icas.png','https://github.com/iebeid/intersection-collision-avoidance-system.git','Intersection Collision Avoidance System (ICAS) is an\r\napplications development for a series of technologies\r\ndirectly linking road vehicles to their physical\r\nsurroundings in order to improve road safety.\r\n\r\nA Java based server client application + hardware implementation (GPS-Microcontrollers), based upon that vehicles can be connected to servers on the streets to be able to control traffic','Vehicle Infrastructure Integration (VII) is an initiative fostering research and applications development for a series of technologies directly linking road vehicles to their physical surroundings, first and foremost in order to improve road safety.\r\nVII specifically covers road transport although similar technologies are in place or under development for other modes of transport. Planes, for example, use ground-based beacons for automated guidance, allowing the autopilot to fly the plane without human intervention. In highway engineering, improving the \r\nsafety of a roadway can diminish overall efficiency. VII targets improvements in both safety and efficiency\r\nThe goal of VII is to provide a communications link between vehicles on the road (via On-Board Equipment, OBE), and between vehicles and the roadside infrastructure (via Roadside Equipment, RSE), in order to increase the safety, efficiency, and convenience of the of the transportation system.\r\nTools: Java, C, Electronic Design',10,2008,NULL,NULL),(2,'Designing a relational database for a video rental shop','Academic','images/db1.png','https://github.com/iebeid/video-rental-data-model.git','Given the data I was assigned to design a relational database for a video rental store given the data columns in Excel.','The main task when designing a relational database is to get it to conform to the third normal form that represents the least redundancy. Tools: SQL, MySQL Workbench',11,2012,NULL,NULL),(3,'A suggested website for the Department of Computer and Information Science at Arkansas Tech University','Academic','images/1.png','https://github.com/iebeid/atu-cis-website.git','An attempt to design a new website for the Department of Computer and Information Science at Arkansas Tech University.','Perhaps the hardest part in designing a website is collecting the information necessary for the website to reflect the entity it is representing. In this website I had to go around collect information about the department and get necessary assets and permissions.\r\nTools: HTML, Photoshop',11,2011,NULL,NULL),(4,'Computer and Information Science Database Manipulation Scripts','Academic','images/db2.png','https://github.com/iebeid/cisdatabase.git','An example SQL Server database manipulation scripts, examples including views and triggers all in T-SQL','For one of my classes I had to design a database that encapsulates all the information of the department. I then had to write specific SQL/TSQL scripts to manipulate and query the data.\r\nTools: SQL/TSQL, Microsoft Visio',11,2012,NULL,NULL),(5,'Graduate Assistants Timesheet Application','Academic','images/dept.png','https://github.com/iebeid/graduate-assistants-timesheet-managment.git','An interactive web application based on the database architecture to manage Graduate Assistants timesheets for the department of Computer and Information Science at Arkansas Tech University.','This project started as a simple SQL database and emerged into an ASP.NET based web app managed by the program coordinator.\r\nTools: ASP.NET, Microsoft SQL Server ',11,2011,NULL,NULL),(6,'International Students Services at Arkansas Tech University','Professional','images/tshirt-face-7.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/imsso-collection.git','A portfolio of some of the things that I worked on during my time as an assistant for the International Students Services Office at Arkansas Tech University.','I spent the Summer and the Fall of 2012 as a graduate assistant at the international student services, creating events, programs and brochures. Helping international students was something that I always wanted to do as a community service in return for the hospitality I found at Arkansas.\r\nTools: Photoshop, Dreamweaver, Excel, Video Editing',11,2012,NULL,NULL),(7,'Masters Project: Visual programming and algorithm animation for genesis programming langauge','Academic','images/thesis2.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/genesis-visual-programming.git','The main goal of this system is to provide a graphical representation of these changes in two ways:  displaying the behavior, of an existing algorithm and moving graphical objects around the screen to simulate an algorithm and the system automatically generates the code.','Novice programming students usually have a hard time visualizing changes in data structures as an algorithm proceeds.\r\nThe main goal of this system is to provide a graphical representation of these changes in two ways:  displaying the behavior, of an existing algorithm and moving graphical objects around the screen to simulate an algorithm and the system automatically generates the code.\r\nIt’s not easy to implement these kinds of systems as it requires access to the runtime environment of an executing program. Also translating the manipulation of graphical objects to code is challenging. A set of manipulation primitives must be defined that will correspond to particular code blocks in the underlying language.  The application of these primitives must be recognizable and the translation must be made. Some options for undoing previous operations must be implemented that will reset the screen as well as the underlying run-time representation. Using Genesis as an open source and simple programming language should make it easier to implement. Genesis implements a single data structure: the list data structure. Accessing and displaying these structures will be challenging because Genesis allows the same sticky note to appear in more than one list, lists can be nested, and lists can be heterogeneous.\r\nTools: Java, JavaFlex, JOGL\r\n',11,2013,NULL,NULL),(8,'Dataware House for a Pet Store','Academic','images/petstore.png','https://github.com/iebeid/petstore-dataware-house.git','A complete data-ware house project with queries using Microsoft Business Intelligence Studio','As part of my effort to learn more about Business Intelligence, I took a dataware housing class where we were asked to imagine a petstore business scenarios, collect data, perform extract transformation and loading the data and build a complete business intelligence applications.\r\nTools: Microsoft SqlServer, Microsoft BI tools',11,2012,NULL,NULL),(9,'Paper submission web application','Academic','images/paper-submission.png','https://github.com/iebeid/paper-submission-application.git','Provide a simple Web-based system for the review of conference papers','Provide a simple Web-based system for the review of conference papers.\r\nTools: Php, MySql, HTML',11,2012,NULL,NULL),(10,'Human Resources Management Tool ','Professional','images/hr1.png','https://github.com/iebeid/human-resources-management-tool.git','A web based tool to manage human resources in any company','A 3 tier, service oriented architecture based web tool to manage data generated by human resources in open source.\r\nTools:\r\nJava, JSP, Adobe Action Script, MySQL',1,2010,NULL,NULL),(11,'Inventory management tool','Professional','images/Jupiter.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/jupiter-inventory-system.git','A web based model view controller designed database management system for business inventory.','Based on Adobe Flash Builder technology with a Java backend and a MySQL database I was able to build this inventory ssytem.\r\nTools: Java, Action Script, MySQL',1,2009,NULL,NULL),(12,'TakolEih: Restaurant guide','Professional','images/owner.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/takol-eh.git','A website that populates the restaurants available in the city of Cairo, also populates the menus and location based on the search.','Takoleh Website is an online guide for restaurants in Cairo City where it provides thorough information about restaurants in different districts in Cairo. A database managed tool for finding the optimal dining place in the city of Cairo.\r\nTools: Action Script, Photoshop, MySQL.\r\n ',1,2010,NULL,NULL),(13,'Python Teaching Assistant','Academic','images/python.png','https://github.com/iebeid/computer-simulator-excel.git','Python Teaching Assistant','Python Teaching Assistant',11,2012,NULL,NULL),(14,'Software Developer at INA','Professional','images/arkansas-gov-logo.png','https://github.com/iebeid/information-network-of-arkansas.git','I was responsible for fixing backend server scripts and database issues for all web apps associated with Arkansas.gov','Applications I worked on include: issues in the Arkansas State Police website backend, issues with the Property Taxes online payments',3,2014,NULL,NULL),(15,'Visual SLAM GPU Implementation','Academic','images/200Kparticles.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/RealSense_CM_VIVE_SLAM.git','My task while interning at Intel during the summer of 2016  was to implement the visual SLAM using Intel\'s GPU technology','Developing computer vision algorithms using a highly competitive Intel proprietary programming library for heterogeneous data and task parallel computing across GPU and CPU.\r\nCombining Intel\'s RealSense technology with computer vision and apply them in virtual and augmented reality applications.\r\nPerforming analysis and tuning on the developed system.',2,2016,NULL,NULL),(16,'Total Solar Eclipse viewer','Academic','images/eclipse.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/solar-eclipse-pinhole-box.git','During a total Solar eclpise in Cairo.','I managed to build a tube pinhole tube so that I can watch the Eclipse without looking at the Sun',9,1999,NULL,NULL),(17,'Back propagation Neural Networks for mathmematical operations recognition','Academic','images/neural_network.png','https://github.com/iebeid/neural-network-math-operation.git','Back propagation Neural Networks for mathmematical operations recognition','Back propagation Neural Networks for mathmematical operations recognition',10,2005,NULL,NULL),(18,'Smart Promotion Tool','Professional','images/white.gif','https://github.com/iebeid/smart-promotion-tool.git','A web based application for managing telecommunication databases after applying promotions to the billing backend','The BSCS tools responsible for the creation of promotions lacks most of the functionalities needed by Morocco Telecom to create customized promotion so there were the need for the “Smart Promotion Tool” a tool which provides ease and black boxing for the user to create a promotion in a friendly interface leaning on back end batches running to apply those promotions. The tool consists of : Online Flex Module , Backend Web services based Server , Java Batch Application calling PLSQL package',6,2009,NULL,NULL),(19,'XLPMOL: An OpenGL Visualization of 2 Protein Models at the same time based on Protein Data Bank Data files.','Academic','images/protein.png','https://github.com/iebeid/xlpmol.git','An OpenGL Visualization of 2 Protein Models at the same time based on Protein Data Bank Data files.','An OpenGL Visualization based on parsing PDB files of 2 protein structures and rednering them in the same coordinate system',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(20,'VisInt-X: Visualizing interactions in Cross Linked proteins','Academic','images/screenshot3.png','https://github.com/iebeid/VisInt-X.git','A WebGL/D3 based interactive visualization of data coming out of the XLPM algorithm on 2 protein structures.','Chemical cross-linking combined with mass spectrometry (CXMS) is an established method in protein chemistry to infer low-resolution 3D protein structures and topology of interactions in protein complexes. Interpretation of CXMS data is challenging due to two-fold identification problem. The first challenge is to identify interacting peptides in the background of non-interacting peptides and the second is to determine the site of interactions. Previously, we developed an algorithm called X-Link Peptide Mapping (XLPM) to analyze and interpret CXMS data. In this report we present VisInt-X, which processes XLPM output to visualize and to interpret cross-linking data. VisInt-X visualizes the results of the cross-linking analysis by including 2D representations of interacting partners, scores and sites of interactions, and by 3D structural modeling of the interactions onto protein structures. VisInt-X is the most comprehensive tool for detailed visualization of the chemical cross-linking data.',12,2015,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVLHPw4s47k','http://ist.publisher.ingentaconnect.com/contentone/ist/ei/2016/00002016/00000019/art00017'),(21,'Information Visualization in virtual environments using Unity ','Academic','images/graph.png','https://github.com/iebeid/info-viz-unity.git','An attempt to create basic graph elements in Unity game engine and visualize it on mobiles and HMDs','An attempt to create basic graph elements in Unity game engine and visualize it on mobiles and HMDs',12,2014,NULL,NULL),(22,'Extracting an Isosurface from DICOM Volume Images','Academic','images/spine.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/dicom-to-isosurface.git','Evaluating various ways to render an iso surface from volume data sets','I used several ways to render extracted meshes',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(23,'Interaction design with Intel RealSense','Academic','images/realsense.png','https://github.com/iebeid/realsense-interaction.git','Simple operations implemented for Intel\'s RealSense Camera','I managed to implement a set of operations on the RealSense color and depth streams: Point cloud generation, depth image denoising using CUDA, PointCloudLibrary integration, Normal estimation',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(24,'Intel RealSense Tracker','Academic','images/ir.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/realsense-tracking.git','A simple VRPN tracker for reflective marker ball configuration that can be set on glasses for prespective trakcing','I managed to to implement a simple tracker server using VRPN, OpenCV and Intel\'s RealSense SDK for front mounted reflective marker balls.\r\nI demonstrated the tracking using a simple OpenGL tracked prespective Scene.',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(25,'RaymarcherVR','Academic','images/raymarcher.png','https://github.com/iebeid/RaymarcherVR.git','The idea of raymarching shaders hightened by ShaderToy website took my thoughts to porting ShaderToy to the desktop','A raymarching shader compiler in realtime that works also for HMD and CAVE enabling live coding of shaders in VR environments.',12,2016,NULL,NULL),(26,'Exploring quad buffered stereo on Nvidia Quadro 6000','Academic','images/quad.png','https://github.com/iebeid/quad-buffered-stereo.git','A simple OpenGL render to explore how Quad Buffered Stereo cards like Nvidia\'s Quadro 6000 work','A simple OpenGL scene rendered in stereo technique to demenostrate the capabilities of Nvidia Quadro 6000',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(27,'TTM Batch: Time To Market Enhancement Tool','Professional','images/java-spring-tutorials.png','https://github.com/iebeid/time-to-market-batch-operations.git','An application for batch telecom operations','Java application which is used for BSCS IX non kernel modules to assure compatibility with BSCS environment. Replacing the uncomfortable use of the (MP, MI, BS, Roaming) Modules in BSCS',12,2010,NULL,NULL),(28,'Team Portal-Time Sheets','Professional','images/vodafone-1-728.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/team-portal-time-sheet-application.git','Designed a web application to upload employees time sheets on the internal team portal (MS Visual Studio C#)','Designed a web application to upload employees time sheets on the internal team portal (MS Visual Studio C#)',8,2005,NULL,NULL),(29,'Contract Layout Printing','Professional','images/Logo_tunisietelecom.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/contract-print-layout.git','Due to the lack of the contract printing functionality in the “Customer Care CX” and based on their trust the business decided to assign the “Contract Layout Printing” application as a – from scratch – task , it enables the user to print the contract after reviewing','Due to the lack of the contract printing functionality in the “Customer Care CX” and based on their trust the business decided to assign the “Contract Layout Printing” application as a – from scratch – task , it enables the user to print the contract after reviewing',6,2009,NULL,NULL),(30,'BSCSIX R2 Migrated Billing System  - User Acceptance Test','Professional','images/Logo_tunisietelecom.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/bscs-migration.git','Providing the client with a highly precise testing and enabling them to clearly know points of weakness based on their trust as highly efficient billing consultants. I was involved in the Customer Care CX web application testing provided that it is the main component of the system.','Providing the client with a highly precise testing and enabling them to clearly know points of weakness based on their trust as highly efficient billing consultants. I was involved in the Customer Care CX web application testing provided that it is the main component of the system.',6,2009,NULL,NULL),(31,'webMethods 8 Migration','Professional','images/orange.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/webmethods.git','upgrading webMethods 6.5 to webMethods 8','upgrading webMethods 6.5 to webMethods 8',5,2010,NULL,NULL),(32,'CRM Offer Assignment Tool Integration','Professional','images/orange.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/webmethods.git','Integrating Customer Relationship Management System with the Billing and the Rating systems','Integrating Customer Relationship Management System with the Billing and the Rating systems',5,2010,NULL,NULL),(33,'Rate plan Instant Migration Handler','Professional','images/orange.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/webmethods.git','Integrating Billing and Charging (IN) systems to provide the functionality of texting the customer after rate plan change','Integrating Billing and Charging (IN) systems to provide the functionality of texting the customer after rate plan change',5,2010,NULL,NULL),(34,'RBT (Ring Back Tone) Framework Integration Layer','Professional','images/orange.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/webmethods.git','A set of web services that provides integration functionalities between the Billing and the RBT framework','A set of web services that provides integration functionalities between the Billing and the RBT framework',5,2010,NULL,NULL),(35,'RAID Information Assurance Software','Professional','images/wedo.png','https://github.com/iebeid/raid-tutorial.git','Information assurance software training and tutorial','Information assurance software training and tutorial',4,2011,NULL,NULL),(36,'Real-time object scanning and manipulation in the CAVE','Academic','images/caveobj.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/realtime-cave-scanner.git','I am proposing real time application inside the CAVE environment that would allow scanning small objects on a custom made turntable using a Real Sense camera that would capture the objects information creating a mesh file (OBJ) that would be rendered instantly inside the CAVE allowing the user to manipulate the object using a Leap Motion Sensor.','A lot of work has been done in the area of 3D scanning through high resolution depth cameras specially generating meshes from objects being recognized as iso-surfaces through using the famous Marching Cube algorithm or other algorithms that has been adopted in the recent years by projects like MeshLab. Recently an idea has been introduced to capture scanned objects based on light field rendering through creating billboard rendered images inside the VR environment in real-time, this method is computationally cheap and efficient however due to the lack of resources it will be hard to implement in the current project. This work does not intend to explore the problems in the field of 3D scanning is surfaces but rather to explore and introduce other ways to capture objects and render them in real-time inside cluster based VR environments like the CAVE. \r\nThanks to Intel’s Real Sense provided SDK it is made easy to scan a relatively small object and generating an OBJ file that can be parsed and rendered using OpenGL. Integrating this real-time render inside the CAVE using a C++ library called VR-Juggler which provides a stereo synchronized windowing system that operates on cluster based systems like the CAVE which usually run on quad buffered graphics cards giving a smooth and consistent frame rate and viewport for stereo images.\r\nVR-Juggler already allows introducing inputs that can either be tracked using the cameras that are already introduced in the system, however introducing Leap Motion in the CAVE might be a first but will throw a whole set of challenges that I will have to face in order to get the system smoothly running.\r\nMy pipeline starts with placing an object on a turntable that is positioned adjacent to the CAVE and by running the program a message will appear directing the user inside the CAVE that an object is currently being scanned, the object will appear instantly inside the environment where a Leap Motion sensor is introduced inside the CAVE, then user will be able to manipulate the object in the virtual space.\r\n',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(37,'Synchronized rendering using WebGL','Academic','images/cluster.png','https://github.com/iebeid/cluster-webgl.git','An attempt to synchronize the rendering with several divs in HTML','On the way of acheiving a cluster WebGL synchronized rendering I was able to sync the rendering of several divs',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(38,'PhotosphereCave','Academic','images/photosphere-topic.png','https://github.com/iebeid/photosphere-cave.git','Rendering panorama images to Photospheres in the CAVE','The project is an attempt to render panorama images to a stereographic projection spheres in the CAVE virtual environment',12,2016,NULL,NULL),(39,'Evaluating the “20 News Groups” dataset against multiple “Latent Dirichlet Allocation” software packages','Academic','images/topic.png','https://github.com/iebeid/gensim-topic-modelling.git','A study to compare the results of two packages (Mallet and Gensim) to Topic Model the 20 Newsgroup dataset','Latent Dirichlet Allocation is a topic model that generates topics based on word frequency from a set of documents. LDA is particularly useful for finding reasonably accurate mixtures of topics within a given document set.\r\nWe will use Latent Dirichlet Allocation to perform topic modeling and discover semantic structure of the provided dataset, by examining word statistical co-occurrence patterns within the provided dataset titled “20 Newsgroups” which consists of 20000 messages taken from 20 newsgroups.\r\nThe messages are provided by the School of Computing at Carnegie Mellon University which dates back to 1999. The 20000 messages represent 1000 use net articles with approximately 4% of the articles cross posted, they are typical postings thus they have headers with subject lines, signature files and quoted portions of other articles, also each newsgroup is stored in a subdirectory, with each article stored as a separate file.\r\nThe unsupervised approach provided with LDA allow expressing the documents in the new semantic representation and queried for topical similarity against other documents.\r\nTo explain more we will dive deeper into the details of these algorithms where vector space model is the algebraic model used for representing text documents. Here each dimension corresponds to a separate term, if a term occurs in the document, then its value is not zero. We calculate the value or the weight using “term-frequency-inverse document frequency” which is a numerical statistic that reflects how important a word is to a document in a collection or “corpus”, this value increases proportionally to the number of times a word appears in the document. One of the simplest ranking functions calculated by adding the “tf-tdf” value for each query term.\r\n',12,2016,NULL,NULL),(40,'A visualization of CUDA particles in OpenGL','Academic','images/hqdefault.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/cuda-particles.git','A simple visualization of particles calcualted using CUDA','A simple visualization of particles calcualted using CUDA',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(41,'GLStage: OpenGL mesh viewer','Academic','images/bunny-scanalyze-sh.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/gl-stage.git','A simple trackball camera based mesh viewer','I used OpenGL to wrrite a simple mesh loader and viewer using trackball camera controls',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(42,'VRJuggler Interactivity','Academic','images/cave.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/cave-vrjuggler-interactivity.git','A simple VRJuggler application to demonstrate interactivity with cubes in a CAVE environment','A simple VRJuggler application to demonstrate interactivity with cubes in a CAVE environment',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(43,'VRJuggler PointCloud','Academic','images/bunny_points.png','https://github.com/iebeid/cave-vrjuggler-pointcloud-viewer.git','A point cloud renderer for the CAVE ','A simple point cloud OpenGL based renderer for the CAVE',12,2016,NULL,NULL),(44,'Leap motion in the CAVE','Academic','images/leap.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/cave-leapmotion.git','An attempt to integrate Leap Motion in the CAVE environment','A simple attempt to integrate the leap motion in the CAVE environment',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(45,'Global Big Data Management & Governance in Health Care Information Systems','Academic','images/cloudword.png','https://github.com/iebeid/data-governance.git','A study of Data Governance in Healthcare information systems','A study of Data Governance in Healthcare information systems',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(46,'A study for data security in National Labs','Academic','images/datasecurity1.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/data-security.git','The objective of this article is to define and describe the responsibilities and required practices for all members of the Laboratory with respect to information security and the protection of the Laboratory information assets','The objective of this article is to define and describe the responsibilities and required practices for all members of the Laboratory with respect to information security and the protection of the Laboratory information assets',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(47,'Using Leap Motion as Pointing device for presentation','Academic','images/leap.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/leap-motion-presentations.git','A Javascript based demonstration of how to use Leap Motion for controlling slides while presenting','A Javascript based demonstration of how to use Leap Motion for controlling slides while presenting',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(48,'Exploring Kinect','Academic','images/kinect.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/kinect-explore.git','An OpenCV based Kinect Calibration, PCL integration and Point Cloud generation and rendering using OpenGL','An OpenCV based Kinect Calibration, PCL integration and Point Cloud generation and rendering using OpenGL',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(49,'Visualization of NYC Open data tree locations','Academic','images/datavis.png','https://github.com/iebeid/rooftop-project.git','A simple visualization of tree locations on google maps','Using D3 and Javascript I was able to render tree data from NYC OpenData to viualize tree locations on google maps and a bar chart of the number of trees across years',12,2014,NULL,NULL),(50,'Exit Sign Detector','Academic','images/exit.jpg','https://github.com/iebeid/exit-sign-detector.git','Detecting Exit Signs using RGB camera','An opencv based program that detects exit signs in building as to later be used in a sqfety and fire escape using the Hololens',12,2016,NULL,NULL),(51,'Emotiv in Unity','Academic','images/emotiv_epoc.png','https://github.com/iebeid/emotiv-unity.git','Connecting Emotiv eeg realtime data to unity','Demonstrated in two scenes mind controlled objects or elevation using Emotiv emotion recognition',12,2016,NULL,NULL),(52,'Evolution Trees','Academic','images/crops.png','https://github.com/iebeid/evolution-crops.git','Javascipt based of vegetation of trees using expression','A text compiler that transaltes patterns to trees to demontration evolution',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(53,'Google Earth Data visualization','Academic','images/earth-data.png','https://github.com/iebeid/google-earth-visualization.git','A KML based visualization of male to female ratio per county in USA','A python and KML based visualizatoin on google earth to view interactively the ratio between male to female per county also by running a cherry pi python server to be able to control the visualization remotely',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(54,'Google Earth in the CAVE','Academic','images/earth-data.png','https://github.com/iebeid/cave-google-earth.git','Inspired by the Liquid galaxy','I attempted to synchronize several google earth instances on the CAVE clusters to render a high resolution google earth map on multiple screens',12,2015,NULL,NULL),(55,'Xpress Integration Website','Professional','images/xpressLogo.png','https://github.com/iebeid/xpress-integration-website.git','Using Adobe Flash builder I revamped Xpress Integration\'s website to a rich interactive web venue.','Using Adobe Flash builder I revamped Xpress Integration\'s website to a rich interactive web venue.',6,2010,NULL,NULL);
